# Paper 2 — Proposal and Placeholder

### Working title: *Consciousness Configurations: an application of Grounded Duality Theory*

**Status: placeholder. Nothing here is drafted, and the sequencing below says it should not be for some time.**

---

## 0. Scope, stated as a boundary rather than a topic

**Paper 1 ends at consciousness and identity. Full stop.** It derives the architecture, tests it against perturbation data, and does not sort what it has derived. Open problem 24 records that the sorting question exists and points here.

**Paper 2 is applied GDT rather than theory.** It takes the framework as given and asks what follows in one domain. That distinction is not cosmetic and has a consequence worth stating in the first paragraph of the eventual paper:

> **Paper 2 cannot repair Paper 1.** Any result here that requires changing GDT fundamentals is evidence that Paper 1 is wrong, not that Paper 2 is advancing.

This is the strongest argument for the separation. It means failure here does not propagate backwards. A theory paper carrying this material would have no such firewall.

